    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "STUNNING 6 BEDROOM GEORGIAN HOME ON 3 ACRES IN MALLOW\n\nSavills are delighted to present Duarigle, Navigation Road, Mallow, Co. Cork a splendid six bedroom detached period residence dating from c.1835, set on approximately 3 acres of mature, private grounds, and extending to c.4,250 sq ft of elegant accommodation.\n\nPositioned just a short stroll from the heart of Mallow and within convenient reach of Cork City (c.34 km), Duarigle offers a rare opportunity to acquire a distinguished country home combining historic charm with modern family living. All amenities are within walking distance including schools, shops, restaurants, sporting facilities and excellent transport links, with Mallow Train Station just 500 metres away. Originally known as Sunny Hill, the property occupies an elevated position on the western edge of Mallow, enhancing natural light and outlook across the surrounding landscape. Built in the early 19th century and extended in the 1960s, the property has been meticulously maintained and thoughtfully modernised, while preserving a wealth of original features such as ornate cornicing, marble fireplaces and sash windows.\n\nA welcoming entrance porch with fanlight leads through double doors into a magnificent reception hall, a defining feature of the home with elegant proportions, fine detailing and a sweeping staircase. To the left, a beautifully proportioned sitting room enjoys a sunny southerly aspect, with large windows and a striking marble fireplace. This connects to a formal dining room, ideal for entertaining, with intricate cornicing and garden views. To the southwest lies a bright and spacious living room with marble fireplace, stove and superb outlook over the grounds. On the opposite side, a rear hall leads to a generous guest WC and a comfortable family room with fireplace stove and large window. The kitchen/dining room is a warm and inviting space, featuring a country style kitchen by Abbey Kitchens, centred around a traditional AGA, and offering direct access to the rear yard.\n\nUpstairs, six generously sized bedrooms are arranged around a bright landing, all benefiting from large sash windows. The principal bedroom includes a luxurious en suite with jacuzzi bath and separate shower, complemented by a family bathroom and additional shower room.\n\nThe gardens at Duarigle are truly magnificent, with large sunny lawns, a superb selection of mature trees and shrubs, and excellent privacy throughout. Private gates open to a long gravel driveway, creating a wonderful sense of arrival. To the rear, a substantial cut stone coach house and stable block, accessed via a traditional stone archway, offer superb potential for conversion (subject to planning). With six stables and extensive grounds, the property is ideal for equestrian use.\n\nHistorically associated with notable Cork families including the De La Cour and Sarsfield families, and later serving as a rectory before returning to private ownership, Duarigle is a residence of true distinction, offering scale, elegance and versatility, with the rare advantage of town convenience."
      },
